Initially, all products have price 10.
Write a solution to find the prices of all products on the date 2019-08-16.
Return the result table in any order.


SOLUTION:

(SELECT product_id, new_price as price -- sets newest price if earlier price change is present
FROM Products
WHERE (product_id, change_date) IN ( -- check price change is most recent possible
SELECT product_id, MAX(change_date)
FROM Products
WHERE DATEDIFF('2019-08-16', change_date) >= 0
GROUP BY product_id))

UNION -- union allows us to separate the problem into easier cases 

(SELECT product_id, 10 AS price  -- remains default if no earlier price change is present
FROM Products 
GROUP BY product_id 
HAVING MIN(change_date) > '2019-08-16') 
